# AT-16 S4: the governed paths need a review from their code owner, so that the QA approval lines, the vectors, the tolerance
# profile, the contract and the gates are not approved by the account that changes them. This only has effect with the branch
# ruleset on main "require review from Code Owners" (see README.md, "One-time GitHub setup").
#
# PLACEHOLDER OWNER: @pawangogia21 is the repository owner, used until a dedicated QA user or team exists. Replace it with that
# team (for example @pawangogia21/qa-approvers) in this file; GitHub also needs the owner to have write access, and the author
# of a change cannot approve their own pull request, so a second account or a team is what makes this control real.

# approvals, vectors, tolerance profile, contract, specification
/governance/                    @pawangogia21
/vectors/                       @pawangogia21
/tolerance/                     @pawangogia21
/json-schema/                   @pawangogia21
/algorithm-spec.md              @pawangogia21
/avro/.enum-approvals           @pawangogia21

# CI, the gate scripts (.github/scripts/*), the gate code they run, and the build bootstrap
/.github/                       @pawangogia21
/tools/schema-gate/             @pawangogia21
/mvnw                           @pawangogia21
/mvnw.cmd                       @pawangogia21
/swift/quicktype/               @pawangogia21

# published artifacts: module poms (dependency versions, publishing coordinates), reference implementation, ports, generated-code
# configuration, vector artifact, Avro schemas
